00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:11.440
will do is we will create the object for database&nbsp;
classes on all the three pages, we will have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:16.560
open that connection, we will have to do the&nbsp;
database operation. And then we will have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:24.080
close the connection in all the places to do the&nbsp;
same and create object for email implementation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:31.280
that we have in all the three pages. So you can&nbsp;
see this is a lot of duplicate code. On top of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.280 --> 00:11:37.200
that, what happens in future, if you change the&nbsp;
implementation of how you access the database,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:43.920
or email, based on the current configuration, you&nbsp;
might have to make that change in all of the three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:50.480
pages, which is a big mess, because right now,&nbsp;
it's three pages down the line, it could be 30,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:58.480
or 300 pages. And the issue here is that on each&nbsp;
page, you will deal with creating the object&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:05.120
managing them as well as disposing them. And&nbsp;
that will be a time consuming effort when we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:12.640
have to do that in all the pages. So that being&nbsp;
said, what is a solution to avoid all of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:18.480
and get an optimal architecture. The answer&nbsp;
to all of that is dependency injection.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:25.440
First, let me show how this scenario would look&nbsp;
like. Again, we will have the three pages. And we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:32.160
will have email and database functionality. These&nbsp;
are the common things that we had before as well.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:39.200
But now we will have something special, which&nbsp;
is dependency injection container. So as you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:46.560
can see, we have got our dependency injection&nbsp;
container that will have an ID email and an IDB&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:53.920
interface and its implementation. So inside our&nbsp;
container, we have the implementation of the eye&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.920 --> 00:13:01.760
email interface and the IDB interface. When any&nbsp;
page will need access to these functionalities, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:07.440
will just ask the dependency injection container&nbsp;
to create an object of this functionality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:16.080
and directly give page an object to use. So inside&nbsp;
the page, we will actually be using an interface.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:22.720
And then dependency injection does audits magic&nbsp;
of passing the object when the website needs it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:30.160
That way, we do not have to deal with creating the&nbsp;
object disposing or managing that object inside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:38.720
our pages or pages will look very clean with just&nbsp;
the interface. All the instance and implementation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:45.680
will be done by dependency injection container.&nbsp;
Now in future if you want to change or replace the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:45.680 --> 00:13:52.560
email class, you do not have to make any changes&nbsp;
in the pages, all you have to do is just change&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:58.480
the implementation inside the email class. And&nbsp;
since we are registering that in the container,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:05.440
next time when we build the project, it will&nbsp;
take the new implementation. So you can see we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:12.080
only have to change in one place. Now. That is one&nbsp;
of the main advantage that comes with dependency&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:18.000
injection. Now in order to use dependency&nbsp;
injection, you can use many third party tools.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:18.720 --> 00:14:24.480
But with dotnet core, we have a built in&nbsp;
dependency injection container, and that has its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:32.480
own advantages. So I hope that you have a short&nbsp;
overview of how Dependency injection is helpful.&nbsp;&nbsp;

